 # FP-Brain

-FP-Brain is a local set of four explicit, advisory skills for reasoning from
-first principles. It helps clarify problems, develop solution directions,
-compare options, and understand concepts without executing work on the user's
-behalf.
-
-## Use the skills
-
-- `$fp-ask` — clarify what you are stuck on, one useful question at a time.
-- `$fp-brainstorm` — develop distinct directions from known facts and needs.
-- `$fp-decide` — compare options against your priorities and available evidence.
-- `$fp-learn` — understand a concept and apply it to the work in front of you.
-
-Example:
+FP helps clarify a problem, examine assumptions, develop grounded options, make
+choices from your priorities, and learn through the work. Invoke `$fp` explicitly
+in Codex once the self-contained package is installed.

 ```text
-$fp-learn
-
+$fp
 I understand button variants in Figma, but I do not understand frontend state.
+Explain it using the form I am designing.
 ```

-Each skill reads the shared method at [`method/CORE.md`](method/CORE.md). The
-skills are explicit-only through their `agents/openai.yaml` policy, perform only
-advisory responses and read-only research, and do not depend on one another or
-on a global FP installation.
+You can request a direct explanation, Socratic inquiry or 5 Whys, change the
+approach, or stop. FP provides advice and read-only research. Building, editing,
+executing experiments, installing or delegating requires a separate authorized
+task outside the skill. Memory is optional and FP never writes learning records.
+
+The canonical package is [skills/fp](skills/fp/SKILL.md); its references live within
+the package. Follow [install and rollback guidance](docs/install.md) for the
+managed copy in user-scope discovery. There is no second same-name repo entry.

 ## Evidence status

-The acceptance fixtures are in [`evals/acceptance.md`](evals/acceptance.md),
-source mapping is in [`evals/provenance.md`](evals/provenance.md), and observed
-results are in [`evals/results.md`](evals/results.md). Structural validation is
-not the same as native behavioral acceptance; read the results before relying
-on a PASS claim.
+[Rebuild status](plans/2026-09-06-fp-rebuild/implementation-status.md) distinguishes
+package, native, installed, discovery, picker and real user-trial gates. Read its
+actual verdicts before relying on acceptance. The frozen suite is in
+[evals/rebuild-v1](evals/rebuild-v1/README.md). Historical four-skill results remain
+in [evals/results.md](evals/results.md), with original source notes and traces
